                        "entry_id": "1a4c2496-f54d-38e7-a539-169fe6ff91a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The European green woodpecker, Picus viridis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e41dfb4f-62c6-4cec-9273-d32b9187443d",
                                "sense_id": "02bd870f-733a-36c1-80b5-9d6c409b1002",
                                "text": "I remember the cry of the wood-peckers, or yaffils, as we call them in that country, going to roost in a pale autumnal evening […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c694797-e0e0-4c0a-9af8-04f0ac6f08ec",
                                "sense_id": "02bd870f-733a-36c1-80b5-9d6c409b1002",
                                "text": "“‘Punched that rotton strap,’ he goes on saying, ‘like a gret ol' yaffle punchin' a 'ollow log!’”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
